    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nRenaming a loaded buffer leaves autoread watching the old file, causing unnecessary timestamp checks and busy-state changes.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nRe-evaluate the watcher on `BufFilePost`. Expose the watched path to tests and assert rename handling directly instead of checking 'busy'.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-19T18:07:42Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42428#discussion_r4309624514"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/42428"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4309624514"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I was wondering if 'busy' is the right thing to check here.\n\nAI analysis:\n\nChecking `'busy'` works here only because the 5s debounce holds it longer than the 3s `retry`. But it's checking a side effect, and that hides a problem: after a rename, the buffer is never reloaded from the new file.\n`nvim_buf_set_name()` and `:file` set `BF_NOTEDITED`, and `buf_check_timestamp()` skips the change check for those buffers. So the `:checktime` that runs after a change to the renamed file does nothing. Once the buffer is written,\n`BF_NOTEDITED` clears, but `BufWritePost` already re-arms the watcher.\n\nSo the real effect of `BufFilePost` is to stop watching the *old* path, which avoids pointless `:checktime` calls and `'busy'` blips. Suggest:\n\n- PR description: \"Renaming a buffer leaves autoread watching the old file\", not \"changes to the new file do not trigger a timestamp check\".\n- Test: assert which path is watched, not `'busy'`:\n\n```lua\n    -- Renaming moves the watcher to the new file.\n    api.nvim_buf_set_name(0, t.tmpname())\n    eq(api.nvim_buf_get_name(0), watched_path())\n\n    -- Renaming to a nonexistent file stops the watcher.\n    api.nvim_buf_set_name(0, api.nvim_buf_get_name(0) .. '.missing')\n    eq(false, is_watching())\n```\n\nwhere `_is_watching()` becomes `_watched_path()` (store `{ path = name, cancel = cancel }` in `watchers`). That fails without `BufFilePost` (the watcher stays on the old path) and needs no `_set_debounce(5000)` or `retry`.\n",
            "commit_id": "2d1f909e7c29543b96467a16f610f375b5a90b0b",
            "created_at": "2026-10-19T01:25:19Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -126,6 +126,23 @@ describe('autoread file watcher', function()\n     retry(nil, 3000, function()\n       eq({ 'after reenable' }, api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, 0, -1, true))\n     end)\n+\n+    -- Renaming must move the subscription to the new file.\n+    local renamed = t.tmpname()\n+    write_file(renamed, 'renamed\\n')\n+    api.nvim_buf_set_name(0, renamed)\n+    n.exec_lua([[require('nvim.autoread')._set_debounce(5000)]])\n+    write_file(renamed, 'changed renamed\\n')\n+    retry(nil, 3000, function()\n+      eq(1, api.nvim_get_option_value('busy', { buf = 0 }))",
